            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Poomalai is seated in the train.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u002",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குண்டுமணி",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d001",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Amma! Then I'll get into the next carriage.",
        "notes": [
          "The corrected source label is exactly `குண்டுமணி`; the stale `குணமணி` metadata is removed."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u003",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "(He leaves. Pandiyan comes and gets into the same carriage. From the book he wrote, 'Vaazhu Vaazha Vidu,' Poomalai recognizes who he is. Then she takes out the tiffin.)",
        "notes": [
          "The corrected Tamil says `போகிறான்`, so the stale English `She leaves` has been corrected to `He leaves`.",
          "The Tamil book title is transliterated to preserve its connection to the earlier title contrast."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u004",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d002",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Please eat....",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u005",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d003",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "No, thank you.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u006",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d004",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Have a little.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u007",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d005",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Many thanks! You eat!....",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u008",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d006",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Which town are you going to?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u009",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d007",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Me? I don't know myself.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u010",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d008",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "You are in great anguish. Such things are common in the world. You should not take them to heart.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u011",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d009",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Do you know me!...",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u012",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d010",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "I do...here... (She shows the book.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u013",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d011",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Lowering his head) What a disgrace, ayyo....",
        "notes": [
          "The source exclamation `அய்யோ` is retained as `ayyo` rather than replaced with a more specific interpretation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u014",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d012",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Don't be distressed.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u015",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d013",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 28,
            "printedPage": 20
          }
        ],
        "text": "Can you understand my whole story?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u016",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d014",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 29,
            "printedPage": 21
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Uneasily) I understand. You, who should have been a bridegroom today......",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u017",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d015",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 29,
            "printedPage": 21
          }
        ],
        "text": "Enough. I should never show my face to the world again!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u018",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d016",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 29,
            "printedPage": 21
          }
        ],
        "text": "But you have done nothing wrong.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u019",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d017",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 29,
            "printedPage": 21
          }
        ],
        "text": "Me? I did nothing wrong? I, who lived bound by honour and self-respect, have today become a symbol of disgrace because of my foolishness. Those who see me spit in contempt; those who have not seen me mock me. Though I had eyes I was blind, though I had ears I was deaf. Without thoroughly enquiring about a deceitful woman, I dressed myself up as a bridegroom and came running like a fool. Me? I did nothing wrong?",
        "notes": [
          "The repeated `நானா தவறு செய்யவில்லை` is rhetorical and is preserved as a question rather than flattened into the declarative `I did nothing wrong`.",
          "The corrected Tamil reads `கண்டவர் காரி உமிழ, காணாதவர் கேலி பேச`; the stale English `those who behold me` for `காணாதவர்` is removed.",
          "The corrected source reads `கள்ளி யொருத்தியைப் பற்றி`; `கள்ளி` is rendered contextually as `deceitful woman` rather than the stale literalized `cactus-like woman` based on an earlier bad reading."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u020",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d018",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 29,
            "printedPage": 21
          }
        ],
        "text": "Be quiet now. Come to Madras and take a little rest at our house.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u021",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s020-d019",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 29,
            "printedPage": 21
          }
        ],
        "text": "Rest? No rest can drive away this pain.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s020-u022",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 29,
            "printedPage": 21
          }
        ],
        "text": "(The train moves on.)",
        "notes": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
